<?xml version="1.0"?>
<xliff version="1.2" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">
    <file source-language="en" target-language="en" datatype="plaintext" original="card_narration.en.xlf">
        <body>
            <trans-unit id="wsw_C4A">
                <source>narration.card_back_pictures</source>
                <target>The back pictures: each back's picture for each pack.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="1ie_jNt">
                <source>narration.card_backs</source>
                <target>The card backs: the variants players win or buy for every pack, then choose for all their cards.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="HQIoI_3">
                <source>narration.card_skin_pictures</source>
                <target>The skin pictures: each skin's for each card, filed under the card's pack.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="VFT1IDX">
                <source>narration.card_skins</source>
                <target>The card skins: what players win or buy pack by pack, then choose for that pack's cards.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="riJ7JSH">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_done</source>
                <target>Save. A reward, a purchase or a code will give this back by its slug. Then give it its pictures pack by pack with Illustrate a back for a pack.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="c5hRw6a">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_effect</source>
                <target>Now choose how it moves, among what the site offers.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="9HS.uSj">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_name</source>
                <target>Give the variant a name, for instance At dawn.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id=".sq5eP_">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_new</source>
                <target>Click the create button, at the top right of the list.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="nxpv766">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_open</source>
                <target>Open the Card backs menu, in the Cards section of the left-hand column.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="zkrhW_W">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_picture_back</source>
                <target>Choose the back the picture shows.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="sKhQjul">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_picture_done</source>
                <target>Save. This pack's cards will wear this picture under this back.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="xwqLw0.">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_picture_image</source>
                <target>Add the picture, card-sized, in portrait.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="r2O9ryW">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_picture_new</source>
                <target>Click the create button, at the top right of the list.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="ujvebZZ">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_picture_open</source>
                <target>Open the Back pictures menu, in the Cards section of the left-hand column.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="DLo_ijb">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_picture_pack</source>
                <target>Choose the pack whose cards will wear this picture.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="JNYDLpx">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_price</source>
                <target>If this back is for sale, type its price in the Price field; leave it empty if it is only given.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="vW0_tsF">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_published</source>
                <target>Tick Published: otherwise the back can be neither given nor chosen.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="n.3ofqr">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_standard</source>
                <target>Tick Standard back if this back is the base one, worn by every card until another is chosen.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="WaOX9C_">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_thumbnail</source>
                <target>Add its thumbnail: the back on its own, card-sized, in portrait, which the basket and the order emails show.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="2QlHUHN">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_thumbnails_done</source>
                <target>Check the thumbnails in the backs' listing. For a few backs only, use the card:back-thumbnails command.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="w8mObLs">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_thumbnails_open</source>
                <target>Open the dashboard: the Back thumbnails tile is among the shortcuts.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="NLHdRSG">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_thumbnails_run</source>
                <target>Click the Back thumbnails tile. Allow a few seconds per back.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="BCB.qLq">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_back_tone</source>
                <target>Choose the light laid over each pack's picture, among what the site offers.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="MCT0d76">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_export_follow</source>
                <target>Reload the page to follow the export on the tile, until it shows the date of the last export.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="aS9ond5">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_export_open</source>
                <target>Open the dashboard: the Export the cards tile is among the shortcuts.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="UiTq7q1">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_export_run</source>
                <target>Click the Export the cards tile. The export runs in the background.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="G.TN_0L">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_done</source>
                <target>Save, then give the skin its pictures card by card.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="CilVNmc">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_name</source>
                <target>Give the skin a name, Toon for instance.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="BaAH2qO">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_new</source>
                <target>Click the create button to add a skin.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="mrEhSxq">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_open</source>
                <target>Open the Card skins menu, in the Cards section of the left column.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="O4fL5FL">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_picture_done</source>
                <target>Save: the card now wears this picture under this skin.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="kzABnfN">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_picture_image</source>
                <target>Drop the picture, card-sized, in portrait.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="bUpuQu3">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_picture_new</source>
                <target>Click the create button to add a picture.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="nMguXZW">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_picture_open</source>
                <target>Open the Skin pictures menu, in the Cards section of the left column.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="IrBR6GL">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_picture_pack</source>
                <target>Choose the card's pack.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="ZKgJ_uj">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_picture_reference</source>
                <target>Type the card's number, GOB 01 for instance.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="QyvADTU">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_picture_skin</source>
                <target>Choose the skin the picture illustrates.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="loDr4g6">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_price</source>
                <target>Set its price for one pack if it is for sale, or leave it empty.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="JeewCqB">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_published</source>
                <target>Tick Published: only a published skin can be given.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="4HEbDp3">
                <source>narration.guided_step_card_skin_thumbnail</source>
                <target>Drop its thumbnail, the skin alone, card-sized.</target>
            </trans-unit>
        </body>
    </file>
</xliff>
